      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hissop_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After the 1832 Treaty of Cusseta ceded Creek lands, Coosa County was formed from the territory that now includes Hissop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hissop_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the area that is now Hissop was part of the Creek Nation’s territory in east‑central Alabama.",
